WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.390
- What really is a problem

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:03.580
and I think it's a developing problem,

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:05.280
we're no longer at the point Dave

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:07.110
where it's Republican versus Democrat.

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:10.912
This is now Washington
versus the rest of America.

00:00:10.912 --> 00:00:13.329
(calm music)

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:22.050
- This is The Rubin Report
and I'm still Dave Rubin.

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:25.120
Reminder everybody to subscribe
to our YouTube channel

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:27.860
and click that fancy notification bell.

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:29.410
Joining me today is the former

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:31.390
American ambassador to Germany

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:33.910
as well as the former acting director

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:36.970
of US National Intelligence, Rick Grenell.

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:39.230
Welcome back to The Rubin Report.

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:40.500
- Thanks Dave, thanks for having me.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:41.900
Good to see you.

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:43.840
- It's good to see you, I appreciate you

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:44.673
doing this my friend.

00:00:44.673 --> 00:00:47.340
This is your first interview
since stepping aside

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:50.000
as Acting Intelligence Director.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.390
So I normally don't do
an interview this way.

00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:53.360
You know how I like to do it.

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:56.620
I like to just sit down
and go but I actually have

00:00:56.620 --> 00:00:58.940
some bullet points and I just
want to just plow through

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:00.820
a whole bunch of stuff with you

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:03.124
but I think the first most important thing

00:01:03.124 --> 00:01:05.870
is you talk a lot about the deep state.

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:08.270
Trump talks a lot about the deep state

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:10.730
and yet when a lot of us
talk about the deep state

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:13.810
people say oh this is a conspiracy theory,

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:17.510
this is made up, it's not really a thing.

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.180
There's no way to define it.

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:21.820
So when I say deep state to you,

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:23.270
what does that actually mean?

00:01:24.693 --> 00:01:26.960
- I think to me what it
means is that there's this

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:30.860
system in Washington D.C.
the federal government system

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:33.480
that basically takes care of its own.

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:36.250
You have to be living in
Washington D.C. to work

00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:37.890
for the federal government largely.

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:39.990
I know there are people
that'll say that's not true,

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:43.800
there's different you know,
offices around the country.

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:45.570
I certainly wish that there were more

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:48.410
because what really is a problem

00:01:48.410 --> 00:01:50.580
and I think it's a developing problem,

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:52.300
we're no longer at the point Dave

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:54.120
where it's Republican versus Democrat.

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:57.720
This is now Washington
versus the rest of America

00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:59.900
and what I would say
that the deep state is

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:03.430
is this system in Washington
that protects its own.

00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:06.424
Everybody who gets a job
in the federal government

00:02:06.424 --> 00:02:09.900
has to live in that area largely

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:14.900
and that means that they float
from one agency to another.

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:18.070
They're dependent upon
the federal government.

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:20.720
The media that lives there is dependent

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:25.070
upon Washington D.C. being
large and big and powerful

00:02:25.070 --> 00:02:27.840
and when Republicans or
outsiders like Donald Trump

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:29.880
come in say you know
what, let's shrink this,

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:32.350
let's cut this, let's change this,

00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:37.350
there is this rise up of
people protecting their city,

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:42.660
protecting the state
that they have built up.

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:45.974
And when we have economic crashes,

00:02:45.974 --> 00:02:47.900
Washington D.C. is never hit

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:49.980
because the federal government
has a bunch of workers

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:51.850
that continue getting paychecks.

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:54.740
When we had COVID and people were cut,

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:56.870
why is it that all of the people

00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:59.320
that were standing up saying stay at home,

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:03.670
don't work, put on a
facemask, don't go out

00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:05.300
and participate in the commerce,

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:07.910
all of the people warning
us and telling us that

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:09.870
were people who had jobs.

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:13.070
All of Washington D.C. kept getting paid,

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:16.381
all of Washington D.C.
workers were staying at home,

00:03:16.381 --> 00:03:17.960
they didn't have a care in the world

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:20.090
because they weren't working
but they were collecting

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:22.060
the same paycheck.

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:26.650
They are unaffected largely
when there is a crisis

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:30.570
and so it's this system
that takes care of its own.

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:32.920
Let me also just say it quickly,

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:35.120
when a job is opened up, let's say

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:37.670
at the Director of National
Intelligence Office,

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:39.590
of ODNI where I worked.

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:42.750
We post the job on these websites

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:47.550
that are only known by
Washington D.C. types

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:51.030
or largely known by Washington D.C. types.

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:53.250
They know the lingo, they
know how to go the office

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:54.660
'cause it's a local office.

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:58.084
They have been the deputy
assistant secretary

00:03:58.084 --> 00:03:59.850
of this and that and then they get to be

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:01.660
the assistant secretary of this and that

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:03.640
and it builds on this oh,

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:08.640
well you have to have the
federal government lingo,

00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:13.550
access and job title
in a consecutive order

00:04:13.550 --> 00:04:15.010
in order to get the bigger jobs.

00:04:15.010 --> 00:04:17.510
So it's a system that
takes care of its own

00:04:17.510 --> 00:04:19.690
and when an outsider comes in,

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:22.140
threatens the whole
system like Donald Trump.

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:23.870
- So I actually wanted to
get to this a little later

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:25.010
but I think it's the right segue.

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:27.730
Can you talk about how that system then

00:04:27.730 --> 00:04:31.070
is linked to the mainstream media.

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:34.420
How every article that comes
out in the New York Times

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:37.610
that is supposedly in
a classified meeting,

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:40.260
suddenly gets to the New York Times first

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:41.870
and then CNN and the rest of it.

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:44.333
How they're actually working in cahoots?

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:49.470
- Yeah, look it's, it's not that different

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:51.810
than say you know, we're in Los Angeles

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:56.380
and so the Hollywood crowd
and the Hollywood media

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:59.320
go to the same parties,
they go to the same church,

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:00.570
they live on the same block,

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:02.670
they see each other at the post office.

00:05:02.670 --> 00:05:05.930
So there's this
institutional system right?

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:10.010
If you're working at say, Disney

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:12.290
and suddenly you're switching jobs

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:15.350
and you're working at NBC
and you get a bigger job,

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:17.150
you're still talking to the same people

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:18.660
in your neighborhood
and you're still talking

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:20.070
to the same media.

00:05:20.070 --> 00:05:24.140
The relationships begin to be incestuous

00:05:24.140 --> 00:05:25.540
and you take care of each other

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:27.600
because you're fighting for Los Angeles.

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:29.480
The same thing happens in Washington.

00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:32.580
So when the media go to Washington,

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:35.670
you know the Jeffersonian
principle is that politicians

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:38.610
and people are supposed
to go to Washington

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:40.190
on a temporary basis.

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:43.330
Washington is supposed to
be this temporary place.

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:45.650
It's now got sports teams.

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:48.580
It's now got huge infrastructure.

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:51.340
It's got systems like a
city and now they're saying

00:05:51.340 --> 00:05:54.460
we should be a state because
we have so many people.

00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:56.720
That's not the design of Washington D.C..

00:05:56.720 --> 00:05:58.820
Washington D.C. is
supposed to be the place

00:05:58.820 --> 00:06:02.300
where you go temporarily to make laws

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:03.900
and then you leave that place

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:06.130
and you go home and live under those laws.

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:11.090
We have a system right now
where the media control it

00:06:11.090 --> 00:06:12.150
because they live there

00:06:12.150 --> 00:06:15.080
and they switch from the
New York Times to Politico

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:17.360
to The Washington Post, to CNN

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:21.520
and all around they
just stay in that system

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:23.610
and they protect their own.

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:27.260
And so I think it's a real
problem and by the way,

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:29.300
term limits is not gonna solve it.

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:31.740
It's an, it's one aspect of it.

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:35.270
But if you limit the politicians terms

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:37.500
to six years or whatever,

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:40.207
you're giving more
power to the bureaucracy

00:06:40.207 --> 00:06:41.940
and to the deep state
because they're there.

00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:45.490
And the person who just cycles
out is the politician that's,

00:06:45.490 --> 00:06:47.540
that's the name on the door.

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:50.730
And the power becomes those staffers.

00:06:50.730 --> 00:06:52.770
Now one solution 'cause I wanna always

00:06:52.770 --> 00:06:54.520
talk about solutions.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:06:54.520 --> 00:06:58.890
- Is that we need to move
some of this bureaucracy out

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:02.550
into the Midwest, into
the rest of the country.

00:07:02.550 --> 00:07:06.340
Why is it, and I think COVID
is the perfect example to show

00:07:06.340 --> 00:07:09.280
when there's a problem,
when there's a crisis,

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:12.370
we shouldn't have everything
based in Washington D.C.,

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:13.620
that's not healthy.

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:16.170
And so is there a way to start moving

00:07:16.170 --> 00:07:18.650
parts of the bureaucracy to Kansas?

00:07:18.650 --> 00:07:21.090
To Missouri, to Colorado?

00:07:21.090 --> 00:07:23.360
To some of the other places where,

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:26.520
then the people who are
making these decisions

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:28.640
and living in the neighborhoods

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:32.923
have more American values
than Washington D.C. values.

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:35.870
- How do you think Trump saw this thing?

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:38.340
Like this is basically what he ran on,

00:07:38.340 --> 00:07:40.610
drain the swamp and I don't
think people really knew

00:07:40.610 --> 00:07:43.100
exactly that meant the deep
state as you're discussing.

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:45.680
And I think they meant, I think
most people thought he meant

00:07:45.680 --> 00:07:47.329
oh drain the swamp.

00:07:47.329 --> 00:07:49.290
Like ah just, just sort
of career politicians

00:07:49.290 --> 00:07:50.570
but not like a structure.

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:52.500
Just like people who we vote in,

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:54.263
just the politicians sort of.

00:07:55.131 --> 00:07:55.964
Why?
- Yeah.

00:07:55.964 --> 00:07:56.797
- Have you ever talked to him about that?

00:07:56.797 --> 00:07:58.570
Like how did this New York businessman

00:07:58.570 --> 00:08:01.360
see that thing that most of us didn't see?

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:03.290
- You know I talked to
him a little bit about it,

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:04.760
one of the things that's
really interesting

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:07.220
about President Trump is
he's always been an outsider.

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:10.430
Even as a billionaire in New
York and a big developer,

00:08:10.430 --> 00:08:11.640
he's always been an outsider,

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:14.960
he's always been somebody
who the system has looked at

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:17.180
with suspect and so,

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:22.180
he has the innate quality to
kind of take on the system,

00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:26.050
take the criticism, be
tough through the criticism.

00:08:26.050 --> 00:08:28.510
Not let the criticism effect him

00:08:28.510 --> 00:08:31.319
and that's a powerful combination.

00:08:31.319 --> 00:08:34.660
I also think it's why there's
a lot of gay conservatives

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:38.060
and black conservatives
who are tough enough

00:08:38.060 --> 00:08:41.580
because they've grown up
against the system of you know,

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:43.840
you and I know this is that

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:46.270
the gay leadership in Washington D.C. says

00:08:46.270 --> 00:08:47.690
that you have to think like this

00:08:47.690 --> 00:08:49.050
otherwise you're not gay enough.

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:52.370
Our friend Peter Thiel
was called not gay enough.

00:08:52.370 --> 00:08:57.370
And so there's this you know,
ideology now about being gay.

00:08:57.500 --> 00:09:00.000
What's interesting about President Trump,

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.230
he recently told me that

00:09:02.230 --> 00:09:06.750
when he came to Washington
D.C. for the inauguration,

00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:10.560
to be sworn in as the 45th President,

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:13.540
he had never spent the
night in Washington D.C..

00:09:13.540 --> 00:09:15.266
He had been there.

00:09:15.266 --> 00:09:16.470
He had been there for the day.

00:09:16.470 --> 00:09:17.760
But he had never spent the night.

00:09:17.760 --> 00:09:21.060
Imagine spending the night
in Washington D.C. for

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:24.960
the first time and you're
spending it in the White House.

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:26.520
That's pretty amazing.

00:09:26.520 --> 00:09:28.420
- Wow, that is incredible.

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:30.310
You know I was gonna do a
whole interview with you

00:09:30.310 --> 00:09:32.270
and not mention the gay thing but since,

00:09:32.270 --> 00:09:33.540
since you threw it out there,

00:09:33.540 --> 00:09:34.690
in the last couple days

00:09:34.690 --> 00:09:36.330
now that you're stepping away.
- I can't help myself.

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:38.072
It's such a part of me.

00:09:38.072 --> 00:09:40.600
- The gay thing, let's
just do it for a second

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:42.250
because in the last
couple days you've posted

00:09:42.250 --> 00:09:44.750
a couple pictures of
you in the Oval Office

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:47.530
and you know, I've talked about you know,

00:09:47.530 --> 00:09:49.670
David and I going to
Mar-a-Lago and meeting Trump

00:09:49.670 --> 00:09:51.790
and how he was so happy
that a gay couple was there

00:09:51.790 --> 00:09:53.050
and couldn't have cared less.

00:09:53.050 --> 00:09:54.670
People have heard that
story and they've heard you

00:09:54.670 --> 00:09:58.100
talk about that but you
posted a picture of you, Matt,

00:09:58.100 --> 00:10:00.810
your partner Matt and Vice President Pence

00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:02.440
and a lot of people will
say all right, fine.

00:10:02.440 --> 00:10:04.680
Maybe Trump doesn't care about the gays

00:10:04.680 --> 00:10:07.972
but Pence really hates them and you know.

00:10:07.972 --> 00:10:10.100
And yet, you describe him as a friend

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:11.080
and a good man and the rest of it

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:12.350
Could you do that in like a minute

00:10:12.350 --> 00:10:14.710
and then let's get back
into the intelligence stuff.

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:17.530
- Yeah he's, Mike Pence
is an amazing person.

00:10:17.530 --> 00:10:20.250
He's a committed
Christian, he's a realist,

00:10:20.250 --> 00:10:24.080
he's somebody who's just
so nice and thoughtful.

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:25.920
We talk about Dietrich Bonhoeffer a lot.

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:29.510
He's, he's a Christian
philosopher that we really both

00:10:29.510 --> 00:10:32.409
believe in and enjoy.

00:10:32.409 --> 00:10:35.500
I feel like you know, I grew
up Evangelical Christian

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:36.333
as you know.

00:10:36.333 --> 00:10:39.130
I feel like Mike Pence
is like my uncle, my dad,

00:10:39.130 --> 00:10:41.900
my you know, many people in the church.

00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:43.130
He is just a good guy.

00:10:43.130 --> 00:10:44.510
He doesn't hate anybody.

00:10:44.510 --> 00:10:47.480
He is so nice and he's just religious

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:51.460
and so we can have some sort
of different religious beliefs

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:54.860
or beliefs on social issues and
still be really good friends

00:10:54.860 --> 00:10:56.700
and I think that's where we are.

00:10:56.700 --> 00:11:00.900
I love him, he always
reaches out to Matt and me

00:11:00.900 --> 00:11:03.163
and he's just an amazing guy.

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:06.290
- All right, now let's jump back.

00:11:06.290 --> 00:11:08.130
We'll leave the gay
thing, was that enough?

00:11:08.130 --> 00:11:09.816
Was that enough of the gay?

00:11:09.816 --> 00:11:12.510
- We'll see.
- Enough of the gay.

00:11:12.510 --> 00:11:16.920
Okay so when you left the
ambassadorship in Germany,

00:11:16.920 --> 00:11:19.680
suddenly all these
diplomats were you know,

00:11:19.680 --> 00:11:22.130
publicly saying all these
bad things about you

00:11:22.130 --> 00:11:24.450
and how you've abandoned
them and blah blah blah.

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:27.260
And basically, I think why Trump hired you

00:11:27.260 --> 00:11:29.040
is you called out everybody on Twitter.

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:30.450
You were basically like oh you know,

00:11:30.450 --> 00:11:33.040
that's not what you said behind
closed doors or you know,

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:34.560
we actually want you to pay for things.

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:36.470
Yes, that's what we're trying to do.

00:11:36.470 --> 00:11:39.050
It seems pretty obvious to
me that in your short stint

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:41.580
as acting Intelligence secretary director,

00:11:41.580 --> 00:11:43.530
that you brought that in.

00:11:43.530 --> 00:11:45.980
Can you, can you talk about
just bringing that attitude in

00:11:45.980 --> 00:11:49.090
and like the type of stuff that
you pissed people off about

00:11:49.090 --> 00:11:50.590
in the intelligence community?

00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:54.280
- First of all I hope that you know me

00:11:54.280 --> 00:11:57.029
and I hope that everybody that knows me

00:11:57.029 --> 00:11:59.720
knows that I am actually
a very nice person

00:11:59.720 --> 00:12:01.603
and cordial and never rude.

00:12:02.600 --> 00:12:03.920
I do happen.
- You laid in.

00:12:03.920 --> 00:12:06.410
You laid in bed with Emma
when she had only like

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:09.440
three days left of life last
time you were at my house.

00:12:09.440 --> 00:12:11.970
So yeah, I can vouch for you.

00:12:11.970 --> 00:12:14.290
- Look I, I am a cancer survivor

00:12:14.290 --> 00:12:16.040
and I talk about that a lot because it,

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:17.630
it really has changed me.

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:19.700
I think I'm a better
person because of cancer,

00:12:19.700 --> 00:12:22.450
because of this terrible
Non-Hodgkin's lymphoma.

00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:26.428
But I hope that I'm
always bringing humanity

00:12:26.428 --> 00:12:31.428
and a heart to even tough
conversations and so I'm,

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:36.470
I'm having these tough
conversations at a time when

00:12:36.470 --> 00:12:40.170
it's really important to be blunt right?

00:12:40.170 --> 00:12:42.950
To be direct, can you hear that phone?

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:44.491
Do you want me to?

00:12:44.491 --> 00:12:45.324
- [Dave] That's all
right, that's all right.

00:12:45.324 --> 00:12:47.760
It's the deep state calling
man, you're in trouble.

00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:48.593
- Okay.

00:12:49.565 --> 00:12:52.580
And so what I believe is
that we shouldn't have

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:54.870
these conversations behind closed doors.

00:12:54.870 --> 00:12:57.240
We shouldn't have them in secret.

00:12:57.240 --> 00:13:01.650
When diplomats were first
pushed to their country

00:13:01.650 --> 00:13:04.370
from the United States,

00:13:04.370 --> 00:13:07.850
you had diplomats that would get on a boat

00:13:07.850 --> 00:13:10.370
and take a letter and they
would deliver a letter

00:13:10.370 --> 00:13:13.360
of what the U.S. policy
is to the foreign minister

00:13:13.360 --> 00:13:16.040
of another country and there
would be about three people

00:13:16.040 --> 00:13:18.150
that would know what that policy is.

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:20.280
We now have changed with technology.

00:13:20.280 --> 00:13:22.370
You get to do diplomacy

00:13:22.370 --> 00:13:24.630
through what we call public diplomacy.

00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:27.810
Reaching the public and
garnering the public support.

00:13:27.810 --> 00:13:30.380
There are a whole bunch
of people in this world

00:13:30.380 --> 00:13:33.830
of diplomacy who still
want that conversation

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:35.970
in the backroom of the foreign ministry

00:13:35.970 --> 00:13:38.050
where four people get to decide what to do

00:13:38.050 --> 00:13:42.210
and the public will get
spoonfed when they are told

00:13:42.210 --> 00:13:46.250
that they are ready to get
spoonfed and I don't like that.

00:13:46.250 --> 00:13:47.300
I'm just a different person.

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:49.860
I want access, I think you know,

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:52.420
when you look at how
technology has changed banking.

00:13:52.420 --> 00:13:55.290
We don't, we no longer go to
the bank and have a teller.

00:13:55.290 --> 00:13:57.670
We get to go to the ATM
or I get to transfer money

00:13:57.670 --> 00:13:59.040
from my home.

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:03.180
It's upset a whole bunch of
industries including journalism

00:14:03.180 --> 00:14:06.060
and so I think it's upset diplomacy

00:14:06.060 --> 00:14:08.270
and the last people that
are comfortable with it

00:14:08.270 --> 00:14:09.103
are the diplomats.

00:14:09.103 --> 00:14:13.720
So they want me to quietly
come to the foreign ministry

00:14:13.720 --> 00:14:18.430
and just talk about the foreign
policy that we want to them

00:14:18.430 --> 00:14:20.450
in the back room, in a quiet way

00:14:20.450 --> 00:14:24.080
and I was tweeting and I was talking about

00:14:24.080 --> 00:14:26.634
how we're developing policy.

00:14:26.634 --> 00:14:28.080
I think that that's better.

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:29.850
I think it's a better system.

00:14:29.850 --> 00:14:31.920
Arguably somebody can
come back and say no,

00:14:31.920 --> 00:14:32.950
it's not a good system.

00:14:32.950 --> 00:14:34.360
I get a lot of people on Twitter who say

00:14:34.360 --> 00:14:36.580
that's unprofessional
or you're no diplomat

00:14:36.580 --> 00:14:38.860
and I look, I can take all that criticism,

00:14:38.860 --> 00:14:40.760
it's silly criticism.

00:14:40.760 --> 00:14:43.580
I think that the people wanna participate

00:14:43.580 --> 00:14:45.760
and I am somebody who largely believes

00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:47.330
that the people are smart enough.

00:14:47.330 --> 00:14:48.990
A whole bunch of people think that people

00:14:48.990 --> 00:14:52.020
aren't smart enough and that
we need to tell them what to do

00:14:52.020 --> 00:14:56.350
and I think that we have a better policy

00:14:56.350 --> 00:14:59.530
and a better system when
we can include the public

00:14:59.530 --> 00:15:02.930
and listen to the public and
respond to what they want.

00:15:02.930 --> 00:15:06.070
- So then speaking about
what the people know

00:15:06.070 --> 00:15:07.900
and can know and can't
know and the rest of it,

00:15:07.900 --> 00:15:10.700
I've heard you talk
about how too many things

00:15:10.700 --> 00:15:11.900
are classified.

00:15:11.900 --> 00:15:14.810
That then we can't figure
out what's going on.

00:15:14.810 --> 00:15:16.747
How do they decide, they?

00:15:16.747 --> 00:15:19.550
How do they decide what
is actually classified,

00:15:19.550 --> 00:15:21.540
what gets unclassified, what,

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:24.160
who gets masked and
unmasked and the rest of it.

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:25.970
This'll probably get us
to the Flynn stuff too.

00:15:25.970 --> 00:15:29.886
- It's such an interesting
question and again,

00:15:29.886 --> 00:15:31.770
I don't think I can answer this question

00:15:31.770 --> 00:15:33.420
without giving a little bit of context

00:15:33.420 --> 00:15:36.330
that the system, the
intelligence community system

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:39.910
and Adam Schiff and Senator Mark Warner

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:44.750
all came at me and said this
guy doesn't have experience.

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:46.870
He is inexperienced and he is,

00:15:46.870 --> 00:15:49.210
he is somebody that we should reject

00:15:49.210 --> 00:15:50.610
because he doesn't have experience.

00:15:50.610 --> 00:15:52.480
Now the fact of the matter is,

00:15:52.480 --> 00:15:55.783
my first intelligence
briefing was in 2001.

00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:59.500
I understand what this
system is all about.

00:15:59.500 --> 00:16:03.030
I have been a receiver of
intelligence briefings,

00:16:03.030 --> 00:16:05.130
a consumer of intelligence.

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:07.730
I've utilized it inside
the UN Security Council,

00:16:07.730 --> 00:16:11.810
I've utilized it in Europe
to move Germany towards

00:16:11.810 --> 00:16:14.330
banning Hezbollah for instance.

00:16:14.330 --> 00:16:16.710
With Iran sanctions
I've used intelligence.

00:16:16.710 --> 00:16:20.420
So the idea that I don't
have experience was silly.

00:16:20.420 --> 00:16:24.460
I've had intelligence
briefings before Adam Schiff

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:26.390
and before Mark Warner.

00:16:26.390 --> 00:16:28.717
Both of them criticizing me.

00:16:28.717 --> 00:16:31.410
I just have a different perspective right?

00:16:31.410 --> 00:16:34.100
I come at it from a consumer of it,

00:16:34.100 --> 00:16:37.750
not somebody who wrote the
intelligence or the assessments

00:16:37.750 --> 00:16:40.070
or been the analyzer of it.

00:16:40.070 --> 00:16:45.070
So, when you look at this from
the outside with fresh eyes,

00:16:45.340 --> 00:16:48.120
you look at intelligence
and you say largely,

00:16:48.120 --> 00:16:49.240
why is this classified?

00:16:49.240 --> 00:16:51.070
I read this in the paper.

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:53.840
Or this is, shouldn't be classified

00:16:53.840 --> 00:16:57.020
just because it protects
the reputation of the CIA

00:16:57.020 --> 00:16:59.163
or the FBI or the NSA.

00:17:00.250 --> 00:17:02.850
There are times after certain years

00:17:02.850 --> 00:17:07.430
when we know something
was going on like the,

00:17:07.430 --> 00:17:09.370
the Russian investigation

00:17:10.310 --> 00:17:12.430
and now we know that it was a big hoax.

00:17:12.430 --> 00:17:14.440
I think that it's really important

00:17:14.440 --> 00:17:17.250
to have the public see from the beginning

00:17:17.250 --> 00:17:21.420
what was decided, what
intelligence officers

00:17:21.420 --> 00:17:25.608
and others believe to
be suspect information.

00:17:25.608 --> 00:17:27.390
What kind of pressure they were getting

00:17:27.390 --> 00:17:29.400
from politicians at the time.

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:32.490
I wanna open this up, largely because

00:17:32.490 --> 00:17:36.440
we made a huge mistake
like with the WMD issue.

00:17:36.440 --> 00:17:39.640
The Russian hoax falls
right into that category.

00:17:39.640 --> 00:17:40.970
Intelligence is an estimate.

00:17:40.970 --> 00:17:44.040
I think there are good people
in the intelligence community

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:46.130
that are working really hard.

00:17:46.130 --> 00:17:48.590
We have some bad apples,
just like we have bad apples

00:17:48.590 --> 00:17:53.590
in journalism and in the police force.

00:17:53.980 --> 00:17:55.830
We have bad apples but that doesn't mean

00:17:55.830 --> 00:17:58.340
that we condemn everybody in
the intelligence community.

00:17:58.340 --> 00:18:00.190
It means we gotta get out the ones

00:18:00.190 --> 00:18:03.420
that are trying to be partisan with it

00:18:03.420 --> 00:18:08.210
and so I was pretty good about
having fresh eyes and come,

00:18:08.210 --> 00:18:09.570
I was pretty comfortable I should say

00:18:09.570 --> 00:18:13.150
about having fresh eyes on the process

00:18:13.150 --> 00:18:14.950
and saying this shouldn't be classified

00:18:14.950 --> 00:18:17.100
and I don't know why somebody did.

00:18:17.100 --> 00:18:19.630
So I would declassify it.

00:18:19.630 --> 00:18:24.630
Or I decided that this period of time

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:28.500
between the election
of Donald Trump in 2016

00:18:28.500 --> 00:18:32.760
in November, and the
inauguration of Donald Trump,

00:18:32.760 --> 00:18:36.750
this is the transition
period where the Trump team,

00:18:36.750 --> 00:18:38.970
the national security team and Flynn

00:18:39.820 --> 00:18:43.580
are starting to get
acclimated to the issues

00:18:43.580 --> 00:18:47.120
because they are now anointed
by the American people

00:18:47.120 --> 00:18:50.150
as the incoming national security team.

00:18:50.150 --> 00:18:52.380
If you look at some of the transcripts

00:18:52.380 --> 00:18:57.380
that I declassified from Susan
Rice and from Samantha Power

00:18:57.520 --> 00:19:00.100
they will both tell you
in those transcripts

00:19:00.100 --> 00:19:04.001
which they were under oath
in the House Committee,

00:19:04.001 --> 00:19:07.450
they said sure we talked to foreigners

00:19:07.450 --> 00:19:10.460
when we were transitioning
from Bush to Obama.

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:12.080
During our transition

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:13.970
we were talking to foreign governments.

00:19:13.970 --> 00:19:16.340
They said that the
difference was that they had

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:19.650
a State Department person
you know, in the meeting.

00:19:19.650 --> 00:19:22.490
Somehow that that was
gonna make a difference.

00:19:22.490 --> 00:19:26.090
I think what we saw with
the Flynn Trump transition

00:19:26.090 --> 00:19:29.600
is that people were
interested in learning issues.

00:19:29.600 --> 00:19:32.320
They were talking like
they were diplomats.

00:19:32.320 --> 00:19:35.360
I think when you see that
transcript of Michael Flynn

00:19:35.360 --> 00:19:37.970
you think wow he's, he's a good diplomat.

00:19:37.970 --> 00:19:40.320
He's trying to calm the
situation down with the Russians.

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:41.770
He's not trying to inflame it.

00:19:41.770 --> 00:19:44.690
He's not trying to say
screw them or screw us.

00:19:44.690 --> 00:19:46.720
He's trying to say, you know,

00:19:46.720 --> 00:19:49.470
let's think strategically about
this and have reciprocity.

00:19:49.470 --> 00:19:52.620
So if we do something then
you can come back and do it

00:19:52.620 --> 00:19:54.630
but let's not go crazy here

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:57.110
with coming at each other's throat.

00:19:57.110 --> 00:19:59.130
- All right, so then for
people that can't get too

00:19:59.130 --> 00:20:01.198
in the weeds on all of this,

00:20:01.198 --> 00:20:03.650
then what is the problem
with the unmasking?

00:20:03.650 --> 00:20:06.410
And really how high up does it go?

00:20:06.410 --> 00:20:07.770
And also, just relative to everything

00:20:07.770 --> 00:20:09.350
going on in the world right now,

00:20:09.350 --> 00:20:12.040
do you think it's worth
spending a lot of time

00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:13.690
trying to actually
figure out what happened

00:20:13.690 --> 00:20:15.210
when we're in the midst of well,

00:20:15.210 --> 00:20:17.150
corona, it's hard to
tell what's real anymore.

00:20:17.150 --> 00:20:20.423
But we are in the midst of
riots and everything else.

00:20:22.250 --> 00:20:24.470
- All good questions, kind
of difficult questions.

00:20:24.470 --> 00:20:27.190
What I would say first
is that unmasking a name

00:20:27.190 --> 00:20:30.250
is not in and of itself a bad thing.

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:33.580
I do think, and the reason
why I released the list

00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:38.420
of unmaskers between election
day and inauguration day is,

00:20:38.420 --> 00:20:40.530
that's a higher bar for me.

00:20:40.530 --> 00:20:44.330
To want to dig down and to
know who's talking to whom

00:20:44.330 --> 00:20:47.340
when we already know who is coming in

00:20:47.340 --> 00:20:49.230
as the national security team,

00:20:49.230 --> 00:20:51.380
you shouldn't be concerned about that.

00:20:51.380 --> 00:20:54.660
Unless you're looking
to play politics and so,

00:20:54.660 --> 00:20:57.930
the idea that you would unmask before

00:20:57.930 --> 00:21:01.600
we know who the President
is, before election day,

00:21:01.600 --> 00:21:03.530
I didn't release that information.

00:21:03.530 --> 00:21:07.310
Because I see where you
could make an argument

00:21:07.310 --> 00:21:10.300
of how you need to know what's going on

00:21:10.300 --> 00:21:13.950
in order to blunt some sort of you know,

00:21:13.950 --> 00:21:15.913
actions from a foreign government.

00:21:16.810 --> 00:21:20.550
But it's different Dave
when we know who's incoming

00:21:20.550 --> 00:21:23.000
and you have the Obama team

00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:24.940
in the way that they were doing it,

00:21:24.940 --> 00:21:28.500
at very high levels and in the frequency,

00:21:28.500 --> 00:21:32.150
during the transition,
they know who's coming in

00:21:32.150 --> 00:21:34.880
and yet they can't help
themselves, they're digging deep

00:21:34.880 --> 00:21:39.690
and then what we know is that
the FBI said very clearly,

00:21:39.690 --> 00:21:41.070
there's not enough information here.

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:44.300
Let's drop the case on
Flynn and the very next day,

00:21:44.300 --> 00:21:46.810
there's an Oval Office meeting with Comey.

00:21:46.810 --> 00:21:49.023
Now this is clear.

00:21:50.080 --> 00:21:53.760
The Obama Administration weaponized

00:21:53.760 --> 00:21:56.210
the intelligence agencies to go after

00:21:56.210 --> 00:21:57.640
their political enemies.

00:21:57.640 --> 00:22:00.390
I don't care what anyone
tries to spin and say,

00:22:00.390 --> 00:22:02.210
that's exactly what happened.

00:22:02.210 --> 00:22:05.830
And you look at the
evidence from election day

00:22:05.830 --> 00:22:08.230
to inauguration day,
that is the time period

00:22:08.230 --> 00:22:11.250
that they should've said okay we're out.

00:22:11.250 --> 00:22:14.270
We're, we're in transition out.

00:22:14.270 --> 00:22:18.380
They are now going to be
out and they need to be

00:22:18.380 --> 00:22:20.610
passing the torch for the American people

00:22:20.610 --> 00:22:23.470
to the next people that were just elected

00:22:23.470 --> 00:22:25.730
by the American people.

00:22:25.730 --> 00:22:28.550
Instead, they were so shocked

00:22:28.550 --> 00:22:31.820
that they developed this Russian narrative

00:22:31.820 --> 00:22:34.736
and I wanna make one thing clear.

00:22:34.736 --> 00:22:39.420
The Russians interfered
in our election debate.

00:22:39.420 --> 00:22:43.970
Largely on social media and
they utilized propaganda.

00:22:43.970 --> 00:22:47.200
I have written extensively on this issue

00:22:47.200 --> 00:22:50.220
about what the Russians
have done in Eastern Europe.

00:22:50.220 --> 00:22:54.650
They constantly go after countries
when there's an election.

00:22:54.650 --> 00:22:58.010
They use propaganda,
a tiny sliver of truth

00:22:58.010 --> 00:23:00.810
and they blow it out to make it completely

00:23:00.810 --> 00:23:02.790
an erroneous story.

00:23:02.790 --> 00:23:06.080
This is what the Russians do,
I am very clear eyed on it.

00:23:06.080 --> 00:23:08.060
I have condemned them, I have written.

00:23:08.060 --> 00:23:10.550
I have some of the, I was
one of the first people

00:23:10.550 --> 00:23:14.310
to write on what the Russians
did against Voice of America

00:23:14.310 --> 00:23:16.810
and Radio for Europe in Eastern Europe

00:23:16.810 --> 00:23:19.740
and so I am very clear on how
they do this in elections.

00:23:19.740 --> 00:23:21.740
They did it to us but that's no surprise,

00:23:21.740 --> 00:23:25.590
they always try to use
propaganda in our elections

00:23:25.590 --> 00:23:28.030
to sow chaos.

00:23:28.030 --> 00:23:32.210
The difference is is that the
media developed and blurred

00:23:32.210 --> 00:23:37.210
this Russian election debate propaganda

00:23:37.640 --> 00:23:41.800
into manipulating the Russian,
the American election.

00:23:41.800 --> 00:23:45.490
Most people will hear that
the Russians interfered

00:23:45.490 --> 00:23:47.240
in our election.

00:23:47.240 --> 00:23:50.300
That's a big jump to say when they've

00:23:50.300 --> 00:23:55.000
clearly used propaganda,
largely on social media to,

00:23:55.000 --> 00:23:57.400
to jump in and inflame our debate

00:23:57.400 --> 00:23:59.840
so that we fight against each other.

00:23:59.840 --> 00:24:02.640
And so I think that the
media did the Russians

00:24:02.640 --> 00:24:04.080
a real service.

00:24:04.080 --> 00:24:06.940
They inflamed the debate even more

00:24:06.940 --> 00:24:11.070
and they utilized the
very small investment

00:24:11.070 --> 00:24:12.883
that the Russians put in,

00:24:12.883 --> 00:24:15.500
and they got a whole bunch of earned media

00:24:15.500 --> 00:24:17.920
from our American media.

00:24:17.920 --> 00:24:19.325
- Yeah all right.

00:24:19.325 --> 00:24:20.158
So if we were to whittle this down

00:24:20.158 --> 00:24:20.991
to its simplest terms,

00:24:20.991 --> 00:24:22.580
the intelligence community
said there's nothing there.

00:24:22.580 --> 00:24:24.690
Then there's this meeting
with Comey at the White House

00:24:24.690 --> 00:24:28.110
and now we know, then this
becomes like a two year run.

00:24:28.110 --> 00:24:30.610
Basically to try to prove
some kind of collusion.

00:24:30.610 --> 00:24:32.400
So if that is in fact true.

00:24:32.400 --> 00:24:35.777
So I'm taking your word
for that being true.

00:24:35.777 --> 00:24:38.470
So if that is true, then,
then in effect you're saying

00:24:38.470 --> 00:24:40.317
we have to investigate this all the way

00:24:40.317 --> 00:24:44.182
and that could really take out I mean,

00:24:44.182 --> 00:24:46.000
pretty much everybody right?

00:24:46.000 --> 00:24:48.812
I mean everybody in the
previous administration.

00:24:48.812 --> 00:24:51.120
- What I think Dave is important

00:24:51.120 --> 00:24:54.270
and what I learned through
eight years at the UN

00:24:54.270 --> 00:24:57.300
is that kind of this
transparency and truth

00:24:57.300 --> 00:25:00.100
and reconciliation is really important.

00:25:00.100 --> 00:25:02.758
When you have a crisis
and you have a problem.

00:25:02.758 --> 00:25:05.300
Let's come clean and I,

00:25:05.300 --> 00:25:08.013
and I fundamentally believe in what I,

00:25:08.013 --> 00:25:09.820
I think that the intelligence community,

00:25:09.820 --> 00:25:11.920
the current intelligence community,

00:25:11.920 --> 00:25:14.010
not the former intelligence community

00:25:14.010 --> 00:25:15.950
that the New York Times
and the Washington Post

00:25:15.950 --> 00:25:18.780
constantly quote, you'll
notice they always say

00:25:18.780 --> 00:25:21.150
a former intelligence official.

00:25:21.150 --> 00:25:23.880
That's clearly a former person

00:25:23.880 --> 00:25:25.380
who was a political appointee.

00:25:26.482 --> 00:25:27.800
- Yeah it's also a source on Capitol Hill

00:25:27.800 --> 00:25:30.010
who could be a janitor,
you just don't know.

00:25:30.010 --> 00:25:34.020
- Yeah, the current intelligence community

00:25:34.020 --> 00:25:37.040
was clamoring for reform
which I delivered.

00:25:37.040 --> 00:25:38.770
It wasn't, truly it wasn't,

00:25:38.770 --> 00:25:40.530
most of these ideas were not my ideas.

00:25:40.530 --> 00:25:41.910
I just said yes to them

00:25:41.910 --> 00:25:44.970
because the system was
saying we need to reform.

00:25:44.970 --> 00:25:47.840
And the current intelligence
community believes

00:25:47.840 --> 00:25:49.240
there are a couple of bad apples

00:25:49.240 --> 00:25:50.470
that they've gotta get out there

00:25:50.470 --> 00:25:52.900
and that they were manipulated.

00:25:52.900 --> 00:25:55.060
And I will say this.

00:25:55.060 --> 00:25:59.790
There were red flags early on
in the Russian investigation

00:25:59.790 --> 00:26:04.480
from a variety of agencies and some people

00:26:04.480 --> 00:26:07.860
made those red flags and those comments

00:26:07.860 --> 00:26:09.280
from people coming forward

00:26:09.280 --> 00:26:12.490
and saying this Russian stuff is not true.

00:26:12.490 --> 00:26:15.930
They classified that
information and pushed it away.

00:26:15.930 --> 00:26:19.000
I've seen that information
and I've called for it

00:26:19.000 --> 00:26:19.990
to be declassified.

00:26:19.990 --> 00:26:22.750
It's a process that's
ongoing, it takes time.

00:26:22.750 --> 00:26:24.750
I wasn't there long enough to do it

00:26:24.750 --> 00:26:28.900
but there are instances
where red flags were raised

00:26:28.900 --> 00:26:32.160
very early on in certain agencies

00:26:32.160 --> 00:26:34.167
and I have requested that
information to come out

00:26:34.167 --> 00:26:35.653
and I hope that it will.

00:26:37.146 --> 00:26:38.000
- All right so just two more quick for you

00:26:38.000 --> 00:26:39.240
'cause I know you're tight on time.

00:26:39.240 --> 00:26:41.960
So the first one is
sort of simple which is,

00:26:41.960 --> 00:26:44.006
why not stay there?

00:26:44.006 --> 00:26:45.660
Did President Trump not want you to stay

00:26:45.660 --> 00:26:47.345
or did you not wanna stay?

00:26:47.345 --> 00:26:48.740
I mean it seems like you're
clearly the guy for the job

00:26:48.740 --> 00:26:51.850
but it was only, you know, it
was a couple of months really.

00:26:51.850 --> 00:26:56.340
- So you know, I've been
in Germany for two years

00:26:56.340 --> 00:26:58.710
and I really decided when we went there

00:26:58.710 --> 00:27:01.280
that we weren't just gonna
have parties at night

00:27:01.280 --> 00:27:03.230
and I wasn't gonna do a travel log

00:27:03.230 --> 00:27:04.610
of how great Germany was,

00:27:04.610 --> 00:27:07.680
I was the US Ambassador and
I was gonna work really hard

00:27:07.680 --> 00:27:09.720
to push on US policy and we did.

00:27:09.720 --> 00:27:13.970
We worked really hard and
I had an amazing embassy,

00:27:13.970 --> 00:27:17.350
foreign service officers
who are truly great people

00:27:17.350 --> 00:27:20.830
who wanna do good work and they
were hungry to do good work

00:27:20.830 --> 00:27:23.850
and it's exhausting and look,

00:27:23.850 --> 00:27:27.190
I, I'm totally healthy, I feel great.

00:27:27.190 --> 00:27:30.590
But I'm also very
sensitive about you know,

00:27:30.590 --> 00:27:32.180
not taking it too far.

00:27:32.180 --> 00:27:36.290
I had a cancer scare and
it was a pretty serious one

00:27:36.290 --> 00:27:37.450
that came up fast.

00:27:37.450 --> 00:27:39.880
I'm still getting checked
every three months.

00:27:39.880 --> 00:27:40.810
I you know,

00:27:40.810 --> 00:27:43.070
in all honestly I think that
has a little bit to do with it.

00:27:43.070 --> 00:27:46.100
I was tired, I had in my mind

00:27:46.100 --> 00:27:48.830
thought that we'd only do
about two and a half years

00:27:48.830 --> 00:27:51.570
and then when the President
called and asked me to

00:27:51.570 --> 00:27:55.197
temporarily do DNI I said 90 days

00:27:55.197 --> 00:27:57.970
and it turned out to be more
than 90 days 'cause of COVID

00:27:57.970 --> 00:28:01.190
but I'm just somebody
that when I have the job

00:28:01.190 --> 00:28:04.010
I don't wanna sit there and
just collect a paycheck.

00:28:04.010 --> 00:28:05.700
I'm gonna do it to the best of my ability

00:28:05.700 --> 00:28:09.700
and when I got in, I
decided to go and reform it

00:28:09.700 --> 00:28:11.540
because people were clamoring for it

00:28:11.540 --> 00:28:14.520
and a lot of politicians
on Capitol Hill got angry

00:28:14.520 --> 00:28:16.400
'cause they wanted me to just sit there.

00:28:16.400 --> 00:28:18.210
You're the Acting, you're
not supposed to do anything

00:28:18.210 --> 00:28:21.640
and I said you know, only
in Washington D.C. are you

00:28:21.640 --> 00:28:24.030
supposed to take a job and just sit there

00:28:24.030 --> 00:28:25.193
and not do anything.

00:28:26.080 --> 00:28:26.913
In the rest of the world
when you take a job

00:28:26.913 --> 00:28:28.510
you actually do the job.

00:28:28.510 --> 00:28:30.470
- Yeah I saw you had a
couple tweets about that.

00:28:30.470 --> 00:28:33.090
People were angry that
you were doing the job

00:28:33.090 --> 00:28:35.915
which is sort of D.C. 101.

00:28:35.915 --> 00:28:36.748
Okay so just one more for you

00:28:36.748 --> 00:28:39.550
that sort of is about
everything going on right now.

00:28:39.550 --> 00:28:42.540
As we watch the protests and
the riots and everything else,

00:28:42.540 --> 00:28:44.593
I think a lot of people are wondering,

00:28:44.593 --> 00:28:48.220
something like that this
doesn't feel organic.

00:28:48.220 --> 00:28:51.390
That antifa which now, it sounds like,

00:28:51.390 --> 00:28:53.080
did the President actually classify them

00:28:53.080 --> 00:28:55.633
a terrorist organization
or that's in motion or?

00:28:56.663 --> 00:28:57.757
Do we know where it's.
